    "markdown": "---\ntitle: add_names\n---\n\n\n\n```python\nadd_names(df, groups=None, scale=None, ref=None)\n```\n\nAdd the unit ``name`` and, for each scale in ``groups``, the name of the unit it lies in.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name   | Type         | Description                                                                      | Default    |\n|--------|--------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| df     | pd.DataFrame | Any table with ``geo_id``                                                        | _required_ |\n| groups |              | A coarser scale or list of them (see ``geo.ancestors``), e.g. ``[\"department\"]`` | `None`     |\n| scale  | str \\| None  | The units' scale (default: inferred from ``geo_id``)                             | `None`     |\n\n## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}\n\n| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                            |\n|--------|------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|        | pandas.DataFrame | A copy with ``name`` and one column per group (the group unit's name) after ``geo_id`` (and ``year``). |\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\ndf = geo.load(\"sdg08\", variables=\"index_sdg8\", years=2024)\ndf = geo.add_names(df, groups=[\"department\", \"province\"])\npx.box(df, x=\"department\", y=\"index_sdg8\", hover_name=\"name\",\n       labels=geo.labels(df), title=\"Decent work index, ~2024\")\n```\n\n\n::: {#a399aa77 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.